From 1b7f55cef342477ba8d4a9eff22e08b3cbf8bde2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:47:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/60] v8: use uint8_t for the Debug booleans visible to
 generated code

12.4 re-derivation of the 9.4-series patch 0016, shrunk by a fresh
audit: upstream has since adopted the byte-flag idiom for everything
else that patch fixed.  ThreadLocalTop no longer has any plain-bool
members (rethrowing_message_ and is_on_central_stack_flag_ are
uint8_t upstream; external_caught_exception_ is gone with the
exception-handling rework), IsolateData's layout asserts are now
macro-generated for every field (retiring our hand-added
builtin_entry_table assert), is_profiling moved into IsolateData's
execution_mode_ (an atomic uint8_t flags byte with its own
sizeof==1 assert), and the promise-hook booleans merged into the
uint32_t promise_hook_flags_ that CSA loads word-sized.

What remains is the original case 2 of the 9.4 patch: on darwin-ppc,
bool is 4 bytes (legacy Apple ABI) and big-endian, so the 1-byte
loads generated code uses on C++ bool flags always read the zero MSB.
Debug::is_active_ (CSA IsDebugActive: Load<Uint8T> of
debug_is_active_address) and Debug::hook_on_function_call_ (address
stored into WasmTrustedInstanceData for wasm stack-guard checks)
are the two survivors; both are only ever taken by address through
their _address() accessors, and uint8_t interconverts with bool
everywhere else.  No behavior change on platforms with 1-byte bool.

Audit method (repeatable): sweep reinterpret_cast<Address>(&member)
accessors in isolate.h/debug.h/isolate-data.h/heap.h and check each
referenced member's type against the width of the generated-code
load; sweep sizeof(bool) static_asserts separately (-> fast-API
patch).

13.6 rebase: upstream made is_active_ a std::atomic<bool> (background compilation jobs read it through Isolate::NeedsDetailedOptimizedCodeLineInfo); the same 4-byte-bool argument applies to the atomic's payload, so it is std::atomic<uint8_t> here.  hook_on_function_call_ is uint8_t upstream at 13.6 already.
---
 v8/src/debug/debug.h | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/debug/debug.h b/v8/src/debug/debug.h
index 25aa32a..2f968ae 100644
--- a/v8/src/debug/debug.h
+++ b/v8/src/debug/debug.h
@@ -601,10 +601,13 @@ class V8_EXPORT_PRIVATE Debug {
   // Debugger is active, i.e. there is a debug event listener attached.
   // This field is atomic because background compilation jobs can read it
   // through Isolate::NeedsDetailedOptimizedCodeLineInfo.
-  std::atomic<bool> is_active_;
+  // uint8_t: read with 1-byte loads from generated code (CSA
+  // IsDebugActive, wasm hook checks); on darwin-ppc a big-endian 4-byte
+  // bool would always read as 0.
+  std::atomic<uint8_t> is_active_;
   // Debugger needs to be notified on every new function call.
   // Used for stepping and read-only checks
-  bool hook_on_function_call_;
+  uint8_t hook_on_function_call_;
   // Suppress debug events.
   bool is_suppressed_;
   // Running liveedit.
